{
  "about": "The CloudKit schema the app at this commit needs in the Production environment of its container. Read by Scripts/cloudkit-schema-check.py (compares it with a `cktool export-schema` file) and pinned to the code by CloudKitExpectedSchemaTests. Any change that adds a record type or field updates this file in the same commit; see Docs/CloudKit-Schema-Deploy.md. Additive only: nothing listed here may ever be removed or retyped.",
  "container": "iCloud.MBO.Fernlet",
  "teamID": "3RTUPF8FFH",
  "fieldRules": {
    "mirror": "NSPersistentCloudKitContainer writes one `CD_<Entity>` type per Core Data entity: `CD_entityName` (STRING), one `CD_<attribute>` per attribute, and a `CD_<attribute>_ckAsset` (ASSET) twin for every String and Binary Data attribute (used when a value passes 1 MB).",
    "recordNameQueryable": "True where the app lists every record of the type with a TRUEPREDICATE query (existing-data detection and every delete sweep in CloudKitDataService). That query needs a QUERYABLE index on the system field recordName, written `\"___recordID\" REFERENCE QUERYABLE` in an exported schema. initializeCloudKitSchema does not add it; it is added by hand in the CloudKit Console.",
    "types": "STRING, BYTES, INT64, TIMESTAMP, ASSET as the CloudKit Schema Language spells them. A field a Debug save created on the fly may export as NUMBER or NUMBER PREFERRED AS INT64; the check accepts that for INT64."
  },
